<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The capability the phone announces on the Wearable Data Layer.

  It is the only mechanism that lets each of the two devices know that the application is really
  installed **on the other side**: `NodeClient.connectedNodes` says that a watch is paired, not
  that it carries Pendulum. The two facts are distinct, they are repaired in two different places,
  and confusing them sends the user to install an application onto a device that does not exist.

  ### `tools:keep` is not a precaution, it is the critical line of the file

  This array is referenced by no code: it is the Google Play service that reads it from the APK
  resources. The resource shrinker, which therefore sees no reference, removes it in release. The
  symptom is not an error: the capability disappears, detection finds nothing any more, and
  onboarding stays stuck on "application missing" on a device where it is installed. Debugging on
  a debug build never reproduces anything.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools" tools:keep="@array/android_wear_capabilities">
    <string-array name="android_wear_capabilities">
        <item>pendulum_phone_app</item>
    </string-array>
</resources>
